---
/**
 * Cancellation & Refund Policy.
 *
 * EVERY COMMERCIAL NUMBER ON THIS PAGE IS MARKED, NOT INVENTED.
 *
 * A refund policy is the one document on this site a client could hold the
 * studio to in a dispute. Writing "50% of the booking amount is
 * non-refundable" would publish a contractual term that binds Rajesh to a
 * figure he never chose, on his own domain, where a client could reasonably
 * rely on it. So the structure, the principles and the process are written —
 * they are true of any production business and true of this one — and each
 * actual threshold is a visible `.lg__tbd` for him to fill in.
 *
 * A placeholder that looks like finished copy is how a draft ships as policy,
 * which is why these are styled to be impossible to miss.
 */
import Legal from '../layouts/Legal.astro';
import { business } from '../data/business.ts';
---

<Legal
  title="Cancellation & Refund Policy | Beyond Pixel Studio"
  h1="Cancellation & Refund Policy"
  description="How cancellations, postponements and refunds work for shoots and productions booked with Beyond Pixel Studio."
  updated="2026-08-31"
>
  <p>
    This policy covers work booked with <strong>{business.name}</strong>. The
    exact amounts for your job are in your written quote; where the quote says
    something different, the quote applies.
  </p>

  <h2>Why a booked date is different from a product</h2>
  <p>
    When you book a shoot, we reserve the date and the crew and stop offering
    both to anyone else. A cancelled date close to the event usually cannot be
    resold, and preparation — site survey, planning, scheduling, equipment
    hold — has already been spent. That is what the terms below reflect.
  </p>

  <h2>Cancelling a booking</h2>
  <p>
    Cancellations must be sent in writing, by email to
    <a href={`mailto:${business.email}`}>{business.email}</a> or by WhatsApp to
    <a href={business.phone.href}>{business.phone.display}</a>. The date we
    receive it is the date the cancellation takes effect.
  </p>

  <table>
    <thead>
      <tr><th>When you cancel</th><th>What is refunded</th></tr>
    </thead>
    <tbody>
      <tr>
        <td>Well before the shoot date</td>
        <td><span class="lg__tbd">studio to confirm</span></td>
      </tr>
      <tr>
        <td>Close to the shoot date</td>
        <td><span class="lg__tbd">studio to confirm</span></td>
      </tr>
      <tr>
        <td>On or after the shoot date, or once shooting has begun</td>
        <td>No refund of amounts covering work already carried out</td>
      </tr>
    </tbody>
  </table>

  <p>
    Costs already committed on your behalf and not recoverable by us — travel
    and accommodation already booked, hired equipment, third-party crew,
    permissions and venue fees — are deducted from any refund at the amount
    actually paid out.
  </p>

  <h2>Postponing instead of cancelling</h2>
  <p>
    Where you need to move a date rather than cancel, tell us as early as you
    can and we will move the booking to a mutually available date wherever our
    calendar allows, without treating it as a cancellation. Amounts already paid
    carry across to the new date. If no shared date can be found within
    <span class="lg__tbd">studio to confirm</span>, the booking is treated as
    cancelled under the terms above.
  </p>

  <h2>If we cancel</h2>
  <p>
    If we cancel a confirmed booking for a reason within our control, you
    receive a <strong>full refund of everything paid</strong>, including any
    booking amount. Where we can, we will also help you find another studio for
    the date.
  </p>
  <p>
    Where a shoot cannot go ahead because of something outside anyone's
    control — weather that makes the work unsafe or impossible, government
    restriction, denial of venue access or airspace permission, civil
    disruption — we will reschedule at no additional booking cost. Costs already
    spent and not recoverable are not refundable in that situation, and we will
    show you what they were.
  </p>

  <h2>Work already delivered</h2>
  <p>
    Fees for work already completed and delivered are not refundable. Where you
    are unhappy with delivered work, tell us — revisions included in your quote
    are the first route, and we would rather fix a piece than argue about it.
  </p>

  <h2>How refunds are paid</h2>
  <p>
    Approved refunds are paid to the account the payment came from, by the same
    method wherever possible. We aim to process them within
    <span class="lg__tbd">studio to confirm</span> of agreeing the amount. How
    long it then takes to appear depends on your bank or payment provider, not
    on us.
  </p>
  <p>
    Bank charges or payment-gateway fees already deducted at the time of payment
    are not recovered by us and cannot be refunded by us.
  </p>

  <h2>Raising something</h2>
  <p>
    If you think something has gone wrong, write to
    <a href={`mailto:${business.email}`}>{business.email}</a> with the job and
    the date. A person will read it and reply. We would always rather resolve a
    disagreement directly than have it become a formal dispute.
  </p>
</Legal>
